A1. 20th Century edition of sweet sixteen. ~ FLAPPER
A6. Pearls come from oysters but this is what a girl gets a diamond from. ~ LOBSTER
A12. Kind of stories told by golfers. ~ TALL
A14. A wooden hammer. ~ MAUL
A15. What young men do after the final "good night." ~ GO
A17. An unlucky stone. ~ SOLITAIRE
A20. Chemical symbol for florine. ~ FL
A21. A bad actor. ~ HAM
A23. A landlord's meal ticket. ~ TENANTS
A24. Crimson Oysters Association (abbr.). ~ COA
A25. This is neat. ~ TRIM
A27. Spikenards. ~ NARDS
A28. The entree of a secret society. ~ GRIP
A29. Try. ~ ESSAY
A31. By birth. ~ NEE
A32. People who either blow out the gas or step on it. ~ FOOLS
A33. Barter. ~ TRADE
A35. Something a man does soon after he buys a second-hand car. ~ SELLS
A37. All flappers do this. ~ FLIRT
A38. An arm full. ~ WAIST
A40. That tired feeling. ~ ENNUI
A42. An American rope. ~ SEGAR
A44. Something a poker player does before drawing cards. ~ ANTES
A46. A convincing feminine argument. ~ CRY
A48. This roars loudly in cold weather. ~ STOVE
A50. The financial condition of the great majority. ~ POOR
A51. Rows. ~ TIERS
A53. This grows over the weak end. ~ HAIR
A54. A sock breaker. ~ TOE
A55. The reward of the patriotic disabled. ~ PENSION
A57. Well-known kind of site. ~ DAM
A58. An indefinite article. ~ AN
A59. Tongues. ~ LANGUAGES
A61. A long island in the Atlantic ocean (abbr.). ~ LI
A62. A substitute for cash. ~ NOTE
A63. An indication of "time to retire." ~ GAPE
A65. What a naughty child is at supper time. ~ NAUGHTY
A66. Despots. ~ TYRANTS

D1. This is what Dempsey once was. ~ FIGHTER
D2. Preposition of place. ~ AT
D3. A French step. ~ PAS
D4. What plays are sometimes founded on. ~ PLOT
D5. Girl's name. ~ ELLEN
D7. Leaves out. ~ OMITS
D8. These are theoretically extinct. ~ BARS
D9. What tailors do if you don't pay your bill. ~ SUE
D10. Abbreviation for the thing that "never runs smooth." ~ TL
D11. A backslide. ~ RELAPSE
D13. What men do at the sight of a pretty girl. ~ STARE
D16. Boat utensils. ~ OARS
D18. This is senseless. ~ INANE
D19. South American mountains. ~ ANDES
D20. What movie heroes always do to villains. ~ FOIL
D22. A Christmas institution, now somewhat superfluous. ~ MISTLETOE
D24. Where the dirty work was done. ~ CROSSROAD
D26. A man is very much at sea. ~ MARINER
D28. David's arch enemy. ~ GOLIATH
D30. Fairy tales. ~ YARNS
D32. Ensigns. ~ FLAGS
D34. Delirium Tremens Union (abbr.). ~ DTU
D36. A buttress. ~ EWE
D39. A schooner director. ~ CAPTAIN
D41. The cake's roof. ~ ICING
D42. The land of rug peddlers. ~ SYRIA
D43. These chaps keep by themselves. ~ HERMITS
D45. This comes in the middle of Saturday. ~ NOON
D47. Sue again. ~ RESUE
D49. Druggist's tool. (Dora thinks this means terrible.) ~ VIAL
D51. Creed. ~ TENET
D52. When anything is this way it's "all wet!" ~ SOGGY
D55. Travel the straight and narrow one. ~ PATH
D56. A kind of beer. ~ NEAR
